[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: Missing [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m C export (in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The test harness dynamically loads the symbol [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m from the shared library. In the C code, [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m is renamed to [38;5;10mSPX_gen_message_random[0m via the [38;5;10mSPX_NAMESPACE[0m macro ([38;5;10m#define SPX_NAMESPACE(s) SPX_##s[0m). The Rust translation had the internal [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m function but never exported it as an [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m function with the [38;5;10mSPX_[0m prefix.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix[22m: Added a [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern "C" fn SPX_gen_message_random(...)[0m wrapper in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m that converts raw pointers to slices and calls the internal [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: Wrong [38;5;10mdatalen[0m values passed to [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m (in [38;5;10mhash_blake.rs[0m)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mblake256_update[0m takes [38;5;10mdatalen[0m in [1mbits[22m (not bytes). The C [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m passes values like [38;5;10mSPX_N[0m (=16) directly to [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m, meaning 16 [3mbits[23m = 2 bytes are processed. The Rust translation incorrectly multiplied by 8 ([38;5;10m(SPX_N as u64) * 8[0m = 128 bits = 16 bytes), assuming the values were in bytes and needed conversion to bits.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This is a subtle translation error — the translator saw that the standalone [38;5;10mblake256()[0m function does [38;5;10minlen * 8[0m before calling [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m, and assumed [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m should do the same. But [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m calls [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m directly (not through the [38;5;10mblake256[0m wrapper), so it must pass the raw bit count, matching the C code exactly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix[22m: Removed the [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplications in both [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m in [38;5;10mhash_blake.rs[0m:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m(SPX_N as u64) * 8[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_N as u64[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m(SPX_PK_BYTES as u64) * 8[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_PK_BYTES as u64[0m[0m[0m
